# Maintainer keys for release tags. release.yml takes this file from the tagged commit and verifies every v* tag with
#   git -c gpg.format=ssh -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=.github/allowed_signers verify-tag <tag>
# (generator/scripts/verify-release-tag.mjs). Without a key line below, every release stops before anything is built.
#
# Format: git's allowed signers file (ssh-keygen(1), section ALLOWED SIGNERS), one line per key:
#   <email> namespaces="git" <key type> <base64 public key> [comment]
# The email is the maintainer's git user.email, which is also the tagger email of their tags. One email per line, no
# wildcards, no cert-authority lines; namespaces="git" is required.
#
# A key is added or removed only through a pull request reviewed by the maintainers team (.github/CODEOWNERS).
# docs/maintainers.md, "Release signing key", has the steps.
git@graspea.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIIqxPD0TotCZgTWqtCI2MBUnz1+rWwsqoRJK0EsqBfR1
